WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.700
- I love though that you
also promote body positivity.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.990
You have a campaign, a
movement, called I Weigh, right?

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.153
- Yeah, it's a body neutrality movement.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.670
(applause)

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.640
- So why is this important to you?

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.580
- So I Weigh is a body
neutrality movement,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.800
it's about getting away from
thinking about your body,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.620
and instead thinking about
the things in your life

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.720
that you should be grateful for.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.680
Like, I weigh the sum of all my parts,

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.870
I weigh, like, you can't measure my worth

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.080
on a weighing scale, you can't
measure your own like that.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.150
It's insane that we still do this to women

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.530
in this day and age, so
it's about, like, you know,

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:33.070
I weigh my relationship,
my contribution to society,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.050
my financial independence, my activism,

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.270
that's what I weigh, that's my worth.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.379
And so it's a movement.

00:00:38.379 --> 00:00:40.545
(applause)

00:00:40.545 --> 00:00:41.760
- That is very cool.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.590
- It's this whole global movement,

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:46.700
where we have almost a million followers,

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.500
and we get five or 6,000 more a day,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.530
of people from everywhere,
from all walks of life,

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.120
who are just tired of being undermined

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.720
and underestimated by society.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.550
And it's this really beautiful space

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.350
that I'm launching into
a company next year,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.010
and we're gonna take
this as far as we can.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.010
And we're changing laws

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.340
and changing global policies together,

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:06.932
and we're just done
with how we treat women.

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.860
- I think it's important,

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.160
because, I think
sometimes we focus so much

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.320
on the aesthetics of
what health looks like,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.270
instead of what actual health,

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.960
like and what's going on inside your body,

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.140
and we just don't know, you know?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.580
So it's like, what's going
on in someone's life,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.760
so I think it's a really
important thing you're doing,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.670
especially because you have
such a big spotlight on you.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:27.200
So thank you, for doing that.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.090
- Thanks, you've been
through some body shaming.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.190
- I have no idea what you're referring to.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.989
I literally am getting
trolled right now online.

00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:40.200
- That's so wild, but I
remember you going through that,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.560
and then very shortly afterwards,

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.550
I gained a lot of weight back in England.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:44.830
I was a radio DJ, by the way,

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:45.880
you couldn't even see me,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.270
people just wanted to know I
was thin over the airwaves.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.930
So I got nationally fat
shamed for like six months

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.520
in my own country, and it
was your response to yours

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.370
that gave me the strength
to get through mine.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.050
- Did I use a word that
I can't say on this show?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:00.883
- Yeah.

